The game follows the trend of GTA III (and above) series, however, focusing more on close combat aspect namely kung fu. You still get guns, but at a very limited capacity unlike the GTA / Saints Row Franchise. Don't let this put you off though. The story and character progression is simple yet fun and at times rewarding. Fights are visceral and fun.
Visuals:  10/10  {Wow, experience Hong Kong at its beauty, well great likeness of it...}
Story: 10/10   {You get sucked in from the get go}
Gameplay: 9/10 {Lack of guns may put others off, controls are sometimes fiddly but not hindering}
Worth your buck especially when its on sale. This is one title you don't want to miss.

Finished my first run through the game and I've got to say it's quite unlike everything I've played recently. Took me about 17 hours and it turned out to be one of those games that keep me awake until 10 in the morning.
It feels and plays like your own personal interactive Star Trek episode. It is your classic "
" with a strange murder, a killer hiding amongst your crew, an ancient conspiracy, aliens, mercenaries, and a whole load of mystery. In my first playthrough I have failed to reveal a culprit, but thanks to the fact that the game has a lot of replay value, I will delve into it again in the hopes of solving the case and do things differently.
It's got tons of character interactions (
), pages upon pages of lore and exposition in the Zenlil's onboard library (
), choices that actually matter and a few twists and turns that I honestly did not see coming (
).
The player is encouraged by the game to explore alternative routes as much as possible. One can reload an auto-save made before a conversation (
) and choose a different option if you are dissatisfied with a result. You don't have to, but you can if you so desire.
Aside from rather long loading times, a couple graphical glitches and small progression issues such as characters sometimes responding as if I walked away from a conversation when I didn't (
), it was a pretty smooth ride.
This is probably not the game for you if you enjoy fast paced shooters (
), but if you think you might enjoy an adventure/RPG/quest mix then give it a go.

I have to make a premise: I'm not a kickstarter backer, I discovered this game thanks to some friends that suggested me to play it. I bought the first PA and it was awesome. The Titans version is even better, althought it still has some problems that I hope the devs will solve.
I really love this game, I think it is one of the best RTS of the last years. It is so funny and entertaining, even if you lose, because the battles are awesome to see. It is difficult at the beginning but if you watch some replays (really nice ingame feature) of the good players you can easily learn how to play.
PROS:
- Massive armies;
- Tons of ways to kill the enemies;
- Lots of different units;
- Lots of different strategies to use to overwelm the enemies;
- Lots of mod that can really improve some game mechanics;
- You can build death stars and destroy planets.
- I really love the design of the units;
CONS:
- The pathfinding of the units sometimes is really bad, especially of titan units;
- The AI is not really good;
- Lack of single player content (the Galactic War mode need some improvements to make it interesting);
- Only 1v1 ranked available (I hope that in the future the devs will add a 2v2 or 3v3 ranked mode, this game is really fun when played with friends);
- On games that runs more than 45 minutes on system with a lot of planets (more than 5) the game starts to go slower.
8/10, it needs some fixes, but if you enjoy RTS this is a must buy.
